@startuml
title DFNS Curator Runtime Signing Flow\n(Full Cloud Deployment — Vault Management Operations)
skinparam sequenceMessageAlign center
skinparam responseMessageBelowArrow true
skinparam wrapWidth 460
autonumber

box "R3 Operational Staff" #LightPink
actor "Curator / Admin\n(Browser SPA)" as User
end box

box "R3 Internal Systems" #LightBlue
participant "Curator BFF\n(Server)" as BFF
participant "Indexer" as Indexer
end box

box "External Identity Provider" #LightCyan
participant "Microsoft Azure AD\n(Entra ID — SSO)" as AAD
end box

box "DFNS Cloud" #LightGray
participant "DFNS\n(API + MPC)" as DFNS
end box

box "Solana Infrastructure" #LightGray
database "Solana Mainnet\n(Vault Program)" as Solana
end box

== Phase 1: Authentication (SSO → DFNS Session) ==

User -> AAD: Redirect to Microsoft SSO\n(OIDC Authorization Code flow +\ncorporate credentials + FIDO2 hardware key)

note over AAD #MistyRose
**RISK: SSO Account Takeover (DFNS_SSO_ACCOUNT_TAKEOVER)**
AiTM phishing or MFA fatigue attack can yield a valid
OIDC session token even after MFA completion.
**Mitigation:** Enforce phishing-resistant FIDO2 MFA.
**Mitigation:** Restrict to managed, compliant devices (Conditional Access).
end note

AAD --> User: Returns OIDC ID Token\n(JWT with user claims)
User -> BFF: POST /session/init\n{oidcToken}
BFF -> DFNS: Exchange OIDC token for DFNS session\n(DFNS delegated authentication)
DFNS --> BFF: DFNS session token issued
BFF --> User: Session established

== Phase 2: Vault Operation — Intent Submission ==

User -> BFF: POST /vault/operation\n{intentType, params}\n(e.g., "Settle batch #42" / "Configure off-ramp")

note over BFF #PaleGreen
**CONTROL: Server-Side Transaction Construction (DFNS_SERVER_SIDE_TX_CONSTRUCTION)**
BFF constructs the Solana transaction from the high-level intent.
The browser never handles raw transaction bytes.
This prevents browser-side JS from tampering with the payload.
end note

BFF -> Indexer: Fetch on-chain state\n(current vault PDAs, batch data)
Indexer --> BFF: Current program state
BFF -> BFF: Construct + serialize Solana TX\nDecode instruction summary
BFF --> User: Display decoded TX intent:\n- Program: Vault (verified address)\n- Instruction: settle_deposits\n- Batch #42, amount: X USDC\n- Destination: Tokenizer PDA (verified)

note right of User #MistyRose
**RISK: Blind Signing (DFNS_BLIND_SIGNING)**
If the UI display is generated from compromised frontend code,
the curator may see a benign description while the BFF
submits a malicious transaction to DFNS.
**Mitigation:** BFF generates the summary independently of browser JS.
**Mitigation:** OOB signing intent verification for high-risk operations.
end note

== Phase 3: DFNS Signing Request + Policy Enforcement ==

User -> BFF: POST /vault/sign-confirm\n{sessionToken, operationId}\n(Curator clicks "Approve")
BFF -> DFNS: POST /wallets/{walletId}/sign\n{transaction: <serialised bytes>,\n serviceCredential: <BFF API key>}

note over DFNS #MistyRose
**RISK: Service Credential Compromise (DFNS_SERVICE_CREDENTIAL_COMPROMISE)**
If BFF API key is exfiltrated, attacker calls this endpoint directly
without Curator involvement, bypassing Phase 2 entirely.
**Mitigation:** Store credential in secret manager with IAM scope.
**Mitigation:** Require WebAuthn approval for all high-privilege ops.
end note

DFNS -> DFNS: Evaluate wallet signing policy:\n- Is operation type whitelisted?\n- Does amount/destination pass rules?\n- Is human approval required?

note over DFNS #MistyRose
**RISK: Policy Misconfiguration (DFNS_POLICY_MISCONFIGURATION)**
Overly permissive policy may auto-approve all service-account requests.
**Mitigation:** Periodic policy audit. Alert on policy changes.
end note

alt Policy requires human WebAuthn approval
    DFNS --> User: Challenge: WebAuthn approval required
    User -> User: Physically confirm on FIDO2 hardware key\n(cryptographic binding to DFNS signing request ID)

    note right of User #PaleGreen
    **CONTROL: WebAuthn Independent of SSO (DFNS_WEBAUTHN_SEPARATE_FROM_SSO)**
    WebAuthn signature is bound to the DFNS signing request ID,
    separate from the Azure AD OIDC session.
    SSO compromise alone cannot approve this step.
    end note

    User -> DFNS: WebAuthn assertion\n(signed challenge)
    DFNS -> DFNS: Verify WebAuthn assertion
else Policy allows service-account signing (low-risk ops)
    note over DFNS: Policy auto-approves.\nNo WebAuthn prompt shown.
end

== Phase 4: MPC Signing + Broadcast (DFNS Internal — Out of Scope) ==

DFNS -> Solana: Broadcast signed transaction\n(e.g., settle_deposits)

== Phase 5: On-Chain Confirmation via Indexer ==

Solana --> Indexer: Transaction confirmed\n(on-chain state updated)
BFF -> Indexer: Poll for operation status\n{operationId}
Indexer --> BFF: Confirmed\n{txSignature, slot}
BFF --> User: "Batch #42 settled — Tx: [signature]"

== Phase 6: Audit Trail ==

note over BFF, DFNS #PaleGreen
**CONTROL: Audit Log Export (DFNS_AUDIT_LOG_INTEGRITY)**
DFNS exports signing event to audit log.
BFF records: operation, wallet, tx signature, curator identity, timestamp.
Logs are exported to R3-controlled immutable store (Azure Sentinel).
end note

@enduml
